module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitted_apply_names_the_ci_principal_instead_of_the_applying_one

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }

data emitted_apply_names_the_ci_principal_instead_of_the_applying_one: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitted_apply_names_the_ci_principal_instead_of_the_applying_one" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: AtCeiling { rung: StructurallyGuaranteed, ceiling_reason: "structurally guaranteed." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an emitted live-deploy apply names a principal by constant -- the CI runner principal -- where the principal that actually applies is meant. The apply has two principals (the CI runner under the fleet transaction, the operator under the operator-local entry), and a step written for one fails under the other. HARM: a step that the applying principal cannot perform fails the apply part-way through its mutations, leaving the host mixed.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a fact in an emitted live-deploy script that depends on who applies (the helper sudoers readback's owner, the post-install roster probe's demand) taken from anything but the one DeployAccess the gated dispatcher (gunbc.host.host_effect_realize host_effect_apply_gated) holds: a constant access, a principal constant, or a second, narrowed copy of the access; an operator-local apply that fails a check an unprivileged step performs; `cmp` or `test` exiting 2 on a file the applying user does not own.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: the applying principal is known before emission (gunbc.live_deploy.apply live_deploy_operator_local_admitted already renders it into the v4 receipt's OperatorLocalApply provenance), but the access was dropped at realize_live_deploy_apply_on_host and the emitter minted its own CI access from a constant. Not a sudo-grant gap: the failing step runs unprivileged.",

    "RECEIPT 1 (srv1 prod, 2026-10-12 ~04:0x): the first operator-local production apply from main c22acb7 exited with 'host_effect_apply: shell exec returned a nonzero exit code (exit=2)' right after '/etc/sudoers.d/gunbc-approval-broker-helpers: parsed OK'. It was then attributed to a withheld memory-cap step; the later rerun passed only because the helper grant was already installed (a Noop), not because the attribution was right.",

    "RECEIPT 2 (srv1 prod, 2026-10-12 20:47:33): the continuation apply from main 547e3dd (#13784's transaction) failed the same way at the same point, after tree-sync, tree-remote and the five-digit mode repair had converged. gunbc.live_deploy.emit approval_broker_helper_grant_admitted_steps had installed the helper sudoers readback at mode 0400 owned by fleet_posix_ci_runner_user (ghrunner); the next step, deploy_stage_cmp_stages_command, ran unprivileged as briansrls. The host was left with binary, tree and unit file at 547e3dd and the loaded unit and process at c22acb7.",

    "CONFIRMED (srv1, 2026-10-12T20:50:22Z): as briansrls, `cmp` of a file against a 0400 copy owned by ghrunner printed 'cmp: <path>: Permission denied' and exited 2 -- the exact exit the apply reported. The failing cmp does not appear in the sudo journal, and the last privileged command before the failure is the 0400 ghrunner install.",

    "RECEIPT 3 (side-chat review of gunb-ai/gunbc#13818, 2026-10-13): the first repair threaded only the principal down to the readback, so live_deploy_apply_script_for still built the preamble from the constant ci_deploy_srv1_access_or_refusal() -- two authorities in one apply. Threading the whole access there exposed a second instance one field over: gunbc.ci.ci_deploy_access ci_deploy_srv1_operator_local_access demanded the operator's GRANT roster (hostnamectl alone, held by the 2026-08-13 operator ruling), so the probe that refuses before any other mutation would have checked one command and let the apply spend the rest unprobed. Its prior passes probed the CI runner's roster as the operator, correct only by accident of the constant.",

    "REPAIR: host_effect_apply_gated holds one DeployAccess. It narrows a copy to the drop-in install's scope for its own privilege verdict only (live_deploy_pre_mutation_access, moved into the dispatcher), and hands the full access to realize_live_deploy_apply_on_host, realize_live_deploy_retract_on_host and realize_approval_broker_dark_install_on_host, which hand it to live_deploy_apply_script_for, the typed retract runner (live_deploy_apply_preamble_on_host) and approval_broker_dark_install_script, which hand it to apply_intent_from_effects (preamble and probe) and, as access.principal, to the readback. ci_deploy_srv1_access_or_refusal and its unconsumed refusal family are deleted. The operator-local access demands live_deploy_spent_privileged_commands, what its apply spends; the drop-in still renders each principal's own sudo_grants, so no grant widens. The ungated dispatcher, which holds no access, refuses all three effects.",

    "CLAIMS (module test.claim.live_deploy.approval_broker_helper_grant, deleted with the helper-grant leg by the Google enrolment cutover; the claims named below were not found by name in it on main before that deletion, so their enrolment is UNVERIFIED and owed re-grounding): the_operator_local_apply_is_emitted_from_the_operator_local_access (RED on main) and the_ci_apply_is_emitted_from_the_ci_access (positive control), both through apply_intent_from_effects with the access supplied; an_apply_paired_with_the_other_principal_fails and an_operator_local_apply_that_probes_only_the_operator_grant_fails (the mutants); the_readback_owner_is_the_name_the_receipt_provenance_carries; test.claim.host.host_effect_apply_witness the_ungated_dispatcher_refuses_a_live_deploy_retract.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent until it refused after mutating (a mixed host, twice). RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed on the gated production route -- every principal-sensitive fact in the apply, retract and dark-install scripts derives from the one DeployAccess the gated dispatcher holds, because each emitter's only source of a principal or a demand is that parameter (gunbc.live_deploy.emit imports the DeployAccess type and no access or principal constant) -- and the ungated route refuses. The claims above are not on the required witnesses path, so they are evidence for the rung, not a gate. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: none for this class on this route.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster; the claims above are NOT currently verified as enrolled: their named module was deleted with the helper-grant leg, and the rung is declared dropped at gunbc.rung_drop emitted_apply_principal_claims_lost_with_helper_grant_module, whose trigger is a living witness re-grounding them in test.claim.live_deploy.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
